  "implementation": [
    "Guardian offers its additional Chaos cost only after its controller finalized a spell during this turn. Discounting the selected cost to zero preserves ready entry.",
    "Boar has a separate free entry_ready choice; cost plans are unchanged. Acceptance attaches an all-player movement restriction to that physical unit until turn end.",
    "Declining Boar leaves other entry-ready grants intact; a replay has a new object identity and fresh choice. Warden does not prevent entering ready.",
    "Canonical hand plays and instructed pending plays expose the choices to automated opponents; JSON false remains absent, and invalid flags reject atomically.",
    "Actual native selection opens a concise entry-choice panel with the consequence beside the control. The board and inspector show the accepted movement restriction.",
    "Mote has brief Beginner and Advanced advice; privacy and read-only tests cover both cards.",
    "Staged payment retains the selected entry replacement; refusal returns the card/resources and does not leak the choice into a later play."
  ],
